            "settings_safety_title": "Safety & Usage Guide",
            "settings_safety_disclaimer": "All compass, surveying, analysis, feng shui and related suggestions in this app are for information and entertainment only. They are not medical, architectural, structural, legal, financial or other professional advice. The app does not guarantee that results are accurate, complete, fit for a particular purpose or continuously available; sensor, AR, LiDAR, geomagnetic and algorithmic results must be verified on site. Do not use the app for navigation, emergency response, construction acceptance or personal safety decisions, and do not rely solely on it for renovation, construction, investment, relocation or other important decisions. Obtain the necessary rights for imported or captured content; minors should use the app with a guardian's consent and supervision. To the extent permitted by law, users assume losses resulting from actions based on the app, and the app and its developer accept no liability.",
            "legal_terms_button": "Terms of Use (EULA)",
            "legal_privacy_button": "Privacy Policy",
            "legal_terms_title": "Terms of Use",
            "legal_terms_body": "1. Service scope\nThis app provides compass readings, sensor displays, AR and floor-plan surveying, traditional cultural analysis and related suggestions for information, learning and entertainment only. It is not medical, architectural, structural, engineering, legal, financial, investment or other professional advice.\n\n2. Measurement limits\nResults may be affected by device model, magnetic environment, permissions, lighting, occlusion, network or system state and user operation. AR, LiDAR, camera recognition and floor-plan inference may be inaccurate. Verify conditions on site and consult qualified professionals where appropriate.\n\n3. User responsibility\nDo not rely solely on this app for construction, structural changes, renovation, relocation, investment, medical care or other important decisions. Users assume all personal, property, construction, business and other losses resulting from actions taken on app content.\n\n4. Paid services\nIn-app purchases are processed by the Apple App Store. Subscriptions renew automatically for the period and price shown at purchase unless auto-renewal is turned off at least 24 hours before the current period ends. Manage or cancel subscriptions in Apple ID subscription settings. Refunds, billing and payment disputes are handled under Apple rules.\n\n5. Changes\nFeatures, algorithms, descriptions and paid entitlements may change with system, device or product updates. By using the app, you acknowledge this agreement; stop using the relevant features if you do not agree.\n\nOne purchase permanently unlocks all features, including family room allocation, unlimited floor-plan reports and scroll exports, and future features.\n\nDeveloper and contact information\nDeveloper: Beijing Changxian Technology Co., Ltd. (北京长线科技有限公司)\nContact address: 北京市海淀区海淀大街甲36号5层5014号-970号\nEmail: support@sdnlink.cn\nOfficial website: https://sdnlink.cn\n\nApp license and sharing\nScope of license: The developer grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable personal license to use the app on Apple-branded products that you own or control, as permitted by the Usage Rules in the App Store Terms of Service. Except as permitted by law, you may not copy, modify, reverse engineer, rent, resell, or sublicense the app. As permitted by Apple’s Usage Rules, other accounts associated with the purchaser may also access and use the app through Family Sharing or volume purchasing.",
            "legal_privacy_title": "Privacy Notice",
            "legal_support_button": "Service and support",
            "profile_data_title": "Family data management",
            "profile_data_notice": "Names, birth data and gender stay on this device and in the app’s shared container. Delete profiles here for free; related room labels then disappear.",
            "profile_data_members": "Saved family members",
            "profile_data_empty": "No family profiles",
            "profile_data_delete_member": "Delete family member",
            "profile_data_delete_all": "Delete all owner and family profiles",
            "profile_data_delete_note": "Clears personal profiles, disables personal analysis and requests removal of legacy iCloud copies. Delete exported or separately archived reports yourself. Purchases are unaffected.",
            "legal_privacy_body": "Effective date: November 10, 2026 · Developer: Beijing Changxian Technology Co., Ltd. (北京长线科技有限公司) · support@sdnlink.cn\n\nCore commitment: The app primarily computes on-device and has no developer backend receiving personal profiles, sensor readings, camera frames or floor plans. Apple handles purchases. Some preferences may sync through Apple iCloud; system backups and files you choose to save or share are handled as described below.\n\nIntroduction\n\nWelcome to TianJi YanXiang (“the App”), developed and operated by Beijing Changxian Technology Co., Ltd. (北京长线科技有限公司) (“we”). This policy explains how information is handled when you use the App and what rights you have.\n\n1. Information and Permissions\n\nThe App asks for the following permissions only when you use the relevant feature.\n\nPersonal and family profiles; report customization\n\nNames or labels, relationships, birth dates or years, and gender that you voluntarily enter are used for life-gua and room-allocation references. Obtain the person’s or guardian’s permission before entering another person’s or a child’s information. Profiles are stored on the device and in the App Group shared by this app and its widget. Family profiles are no longer automatically uploaded to or restored from iCloud.\n\nCustom client names, report signatures and seal text personalize reports. The most recently applied values are kept locally. Clear the fields in the scroll editor and apply to remove them; delete previously generated or shared reports separately.\n\nMotion and Direction Sensors\n\nUse: Accelerometer, gyroscope, and magnetometer data drive the compass dial, level, and bearing readings. Storage: Raw sensor readings are processed in device memory in real time and are not sent to developer servers. Field records and reports you save may include calculated results such as bearings.\n\nLocation (While Using the App)\n\nUse: Latitude, longitude, and elevation are used on-device with the World Magnetic Model (WMM) to calculate magnetic declination, local true solar time, and seasonal terms. Storage: Calculated on-device without background location-history tracking. Reports and survey images you choose to save or share may include the current location or coordinates; review them before sharing.\n\nCamera\n\nUse: Only for live preview and spatial alignment in the AR survey feature. Storage: Frames are processed locally in real time, without automatic recording or upload to developer servers. Survey snapshots you choose to capture, save or share may include camera images and are written to local archives, Photos or your selected sharing destination.\n\nLiDAR / RoomPlan Room Scanning\n\nUse: On supported devices, the App uses Apple’s ARKit and RoomPlan frameworks to scan rooms and produce spatial geometry. Storage: Scan data is processed on-device. If you export or share spatial files, they may contain building structure, orientation, or location information; whether to share them is your decision.\n\nSaved surveys may also contain room geometry, doors and windows, directions, annotation points and ARWorldMap data used to restore spatial positioning. These archives are stored locally; manage exported, backed-up or shared copies where they are stored.\n\nPhotos\n\nRead: Lets you pick a blueprint or floor-plan photo for analysis. Write: Lets you save generated reports, culture scrolls, daily auspicious sign cards, or watermarked survey images to your photo library. We access only the images you explicitly select.\n\nLocal Notifications (Optional)\n\nUse: Only when you actively enable “24 Solar Terms Reminders” or “Auspicious Day Reminders”, the App schedules local alerts via iOS UNUserNotificationCenter. Storage: Computed and triggered entirely on-device without remote push servers or push token uploads.\n\nIn-App Purchases (StoreKit)\n\nUse: Purchase and restoration of the TianJi YanXiang Annual Membership (auto-renewable subscription), TianJi YanXiang Pro (Lifetime), Floor-Plan Reference Report (single), and Watermark-Free Culture Scroll (single). Storage: Apple StoreKit handles payments and transaction verification. An integrity-checked entitlement mirror and consumable balances are stored in local UserDefaults; verification keys are kept in Keychain. We do not receive card details. Verification keys are eligible for migration through Apple-supported system backups; balances and keys must be restored together. If an older backup lacks the original key, records are kept and support is offered; unverified records do not generate new credits. We do not track advertising.\n\nRestore Purchases uses Apple verification for active annual subscriptions and lifetime access. Single-use consumable credits are not reissued through Apple restoration; backup migration requires both the balance records and their original verification key.\n\n2. Third-Party SDKs and Data Sharing\n\nThe app has no third-party advertising or analytics SDKs, does not collect IDFA, does not track across apps or websites, and does not sell or rent your data. Payments, iCloud and system backups handled by Apple, and recipients you choose when sharing, process data within the scope described here and under the applicable service rules.\n\n3. Data Retention and Security\n\nFloor-plan drafts, survey archives, reports and settings are stored in the iOS app sandbox or the App Group shared with the widget, depending on the feature. Purchase rights and credits are stored in integrity-checked local UserDefaults; the verification key is stored in Keychain. Not all archives are stored in Keychain. Data remains until deleted. After app removal, treatment of the sandbox, shared container and Keychain follows iOS behavior; removal does not automatically delete Apple cloud copies, system backups, Photos or copies held by others.\n\nApple iCloud, system backups and migration\n\nCompass-lock preferences and action lists may sync through Apple’s iCloud key-value store when supported by the distributed app and system settings. This update stops automatic cloud sync of personal family profiles. Deleting a profile also requests removal of accessible legacy iCloud profile copies; offline deletion may finish syncing after reconnection.\n\nPrivacy API purposes\n\nUserDefaults stores settings for this app and its App Group; file timestamps manage local survey files; system uptime measures AR refresh intervals. There are no advertising or third-party analytics SDKs, no cross-app tracking and no upload of profiles, plans or camera frames to developer servers.\n\n4. Your Rights and Choices\n\n• Withdraw permissions: You can turn off camera, location, or photo access at any time in iOS Settings → Privacy & Security. The related feature will stop working; other features are unaffected.\n\n• Deletion: Data remains until you delete it. With or without a paid membership, open Settings → Family data management to delete individual members or clear all owner and family profiles and disable personal analysis. This removes local, shared-container and accessible legacy iCloud profile copies. Previously exported, shared or separately archived copies must be deleted where they are stored.\n\n• Questions and requests: For questions about data handling or to exercise rights available under applicable law, email support@sdnlink.cn.\n\n• Subscriptions: Subscriptions, refunds, and billing are handled by Apple; manage them in Settings → Apple ID → Subscriptions.\n\nRevoke location, camera, Photos and notification permissions in iOS Settings; only the related features are affected. Deleting the app does not cancel a subscription; manage it in Apple ID settings. Apple backups, iCloud and shared files are handled by Apple or recipients under their own rules. Contact support@sdnlink.cn for privacy or deletion requests.\n\n5. Children’s Privacy\n\nThe app is not directed to independent use by children under 13. Parents or guardians may enter a child’s name or label, birth information and gender for family room-allocation references. Obtain appropriate permission and enter only necessary information. These profiles follow the local family-data rules and can be deleted through the free family data management screen. Contact support@sdnlink.cn for assistance.\n\n6. Policy Changes and Contact\n\nWe may update this policy from time to time and will revise the effective date and announce changes in the App’s release notes or on this page. Questions or complaints: support@sdnlink.cn. Developer: Beijing Changxian Technology Co., Ltd. (北京长线科技有限公司).\n\nDeveloper: Beijing Changxian Technology Co., Ltd. (北京长线科技有限公司)\n\nContact address: 北京市海淀区海淀大街甲36号5层5014号-970号\n\nEmail: support@sdnlink.cn\n\nOfficial website: https://sdnlink.cn",
            "legal_compliance_button": "Safety & Compliance",
            "legal_compliance_title": "Safety & Compliance",
            "legal_compliance_body": "1. Service scope\nThis app provides compass readings, magnetic and true-north conversion, AR scene tools, LiDAR/RoomPlan spatial surveying, floor-plan analysis, traditional cultural analysis and related suggestions. All results are for information, learning and entertainment only. They are not medical, architectural, structural, engineering, legal, financial, investment, navigation or other professional advice.\n\n2. Measurement and algorithm limits\nReadings and analysis may be affected by device model, sensor performance, magnetic interference, metal objects, electrical equipment, device attitude, permissions, lighting, occlusion, network and system state. Camera recognition, AR, LiDAR, RoomPlan, floor-plan recognition and bearing calculations may be inaccurate, delayed or unavailable. Twenty-four mountains, solar terms, magnetic declination and traditional metaphysics results are algorithmic estimates and are not guaranteed to be accurate, complete, real-time or suitable for a particular situation. Verify important conclusions on site and consult qualified professionals when needed.\n\n3. Prohibited or unsuitable uses\nDo not use this app for vehicle, marine, aviation or outdoor navigation; emergency response, fire safety, medical decisions, construction layout, load-bearing structure decisions, engineering acceptance, building safety assessment, land surveying or personal safety decisions. AR/LiDAR output cannot replace professional architectural, surveying, structural or fire-safety work.\n\n4. User responsibility and losses\nUsers must make independent judgments based on actual conditions, confirm permissions and sensor status, and remain responsible for renovation, construction, relocation, investment, business or other actions based on app content. To the extent permitted by law, users bear personal, property, construction, business and other losses caused by misunderstanding, misuse, device failure, environmental interference, algorithmic error or third-party service interruption.\n\n5. Content authorization and intellectual property\nBefore importing floor plans, photos, videos or other materials, users must have the necessary rights or permission. Do not infringe privacy, publicity, copyright, trade secrets or other rights. Reports and images generated by the app are for lawful personal use; do not use them for deceptive advertising, misleading others or unlawful activity without authorization.\n\n6. Permissions, privacy and on-device processing\nLocation, motion sensor, magnetometer, camera and photo permissions are requested only when the related feature is used. In the current version, camera frames, floor plans and AR/vision analysis are mainly processed on the device. Manage permissions in iOS Settings. Disabling a permission may disable related features; the app will not bypass system authorization.\n\n7. Third-party platforms and in-app purchases\nIn-app purchases are processed by the Apple App Store. Price, tax, availability, refunds, billing, subscription renewal and cancellation follow the purchase screen and Apple rules. Subscription management and restoration require the relevant Apple ID. Apple, iOS, ARKit, RoomPlan, Core Location and other system services are provided by their respective providers; the app does not guarantee continuous availability.\n\n8. Minors\nMinors should use the app with a guardian's consent and supervision. Guardians should help them understand measurement, payment and privacy risks. Do not collect, publish or distribute sensitive information about minors through the app.\n\n9. Updates and feedback\nFeatures, algorithms, permissions, paid entitlements and descriptions may change due to system, device, legal or product updates. If servers, accounts, analytics or other data processing are added, the privacy notice will be updated and required authorization obtained. Read the latest Terms of Use, Privacy Notice and this Compliance & Safety Notice before use. Contact support through the app listing for questions.",
